\label{thm:main}
Let $1<s\le2$ and let $E\subset C[0,1]$ be finite-dimensional, with $E\setminus\{0\}\subsetH_s[0,1]$. Then there is a closed complemented subspace $F\subset C[0,1]$ such that
\[E\subset F,\qquad F\simeq c_0,\qquad F\setminus\{0\}\subsetH_s[0,1].\]

\label{thm:threshold}
Let $1<s\le2$. For every cardinal $1\le\alpha\le\mathfrak c$,
\[H_s[0,1]\text{ is }(\alpha,\mathfrak c)\text{-spaceable}
\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad \alpha<\aleph_0.\]

\label{lem:localization}
Let $1<s\le2$ and let $E\subset C[0,1]$ be finite-dimensional, with $E\setminus\{0\}\subsetH_s[0,1]$. There is a compact set $K\subset[0,1]$ such that $\dim_{\rm H} K=s-1$ and
\begin{equation}\label{eq:outside}
\dim_{\rm H} G_h([0,1]\setminus K)=s
\qquad(h\in E\setminus\{0\}).
\end{equation}
